# Shared public GET + after (LAW)

Canonical: `AIRULES/03-MODULES-AND-ROUTING.md` “Shared public files when another module may already own GET”. CMS packs: `app/modules/CMS/AIRULES/10-SHARED-PUBLIC-FEEDS.md`.

The first matching `Router::get` wins. A later GET on `/sitemap.xml` is a silent no-op if CMS (or anyone) already claimed it.

## MUST

- Claim GET with a **passthrough** that returns a **string** (`''` is OK) — never a `Response` (that skips after). This is the fallback when the path is still free.
- Put merge logic in `->after(...)` **and** the same handler on global `Router::after(['GET'], '/sitemap.xml', ...)`. After is the foolproof layer: valid body → append; empty/invalid → generate the whole file.
- Same for `/robots.txt`, `/rss.xml`, `/llms.txt`.
- Wake `initializeRoutes()` with those paths. After is **idempotent**.
- After PHPDoc: `CRCchecking — none`. Return a string. Set Content-Type when you generate.

## MUST NOT

- `Router::get` alone on a path another module may own
- Skip GET passthrough because a host “might” be installed (after still needs GET empty when the path is free)
- `Events::trigger` to append XML
- `Response` from GET or after if others still need after
- `Router::reset(true)` to steal the path
- Extender-replace the host feed just to append (Extender = full replace)
